    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5705d649-f138-537c-a3df-f1cf511f9d91",
      ":question/problem": "$\\int \\frac{2}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let $u=x+5.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
